From: Michael Holmboe <michael.holmboe@umu.se>
Date: Wed, 25 Nov 2026 14:48:27 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] Separate the SED and Predom calculations from their windows

SedCalc and PredomCalc hold the calculation path of SED and Predom
(command-line options, reading the data file, HaltaFall, plot and table
output) without Swing or AWT. The methods are moved from SED.java and
Predom.java; values that were read back from widgets (number of steps,
text height, activity-coefficient model, tolerance, temperature and
pressure) are fields, and message boxes go through a small Display
interface that the frames implement. The frames keep the widgets,
events, dialogs and the SwingWorker. initComponents() and the .form
files are unchanged.

Without a display (java.awt.headless=true), SED.main and Predom.main
make the diagram without opening a window and exit with status 1 if no
plot file was written.

Plot files, table files and console output are identical to master on
7 SED and 6 Predom test inputs, with and without a window.
